> [Professor] Colin Butler is based at the Faculty of Health,[ University] of Canberra. He is a medical graduate ([University] of[ Newcastle])[ with] post[graduate qualifications in epidemiology] ([London)] and[ population] health ([Australian] National University). His interest in[ population] and environment dates[ from] his[ experiences] in[ Nigeria as] a[ student in 1985; he] worked in areas that were then[ peaceful] but are[ now] frequently scenes of atrocity. In 1989[,] Colin and[ his] late wife, Susan, co-[founded] the NGO BODHI (Benevolent Organisation for Development, Health & Insight). In 2014[, he co]-[founded] Health-Earth. Colin has published widely, including on health,[ population], sustainability, conflict and justice. In 2009[, he] was named one of ‘100 doctors for the planet’ by[ the] French Environmental Health Association. Colin edited ‘Climate change and global health’ (CABI, 2014) and is senior editor of ‘Health of people, places and planet. Reflections[ based] on[ Tony] McMichael’s four decades of[ contribution] to epidemiological understanding’ ([AN]U Press).

